From b214c2746d08882ed40ea292fa17ad2d37257da9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JimmyBlunt <jo@paso-music.de>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 00:44:42 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 03/15] Extract layout resolution and loop start in Preview
 (local #9002)

Behaviour-preserving refactor ahead of FastLED Patterns: the main preview
effect now has two local helpers, resolveActiveLayout(nativeDim) (resolve,
reflect corrections, publish display/map dims, label, solid eligibility)
and startLoop(layout, handle, shim, clock, renderCompatibility) (renderer,
paint/paintPacked wrappers, external pixel output, render loop, cleanup).
The Pixelblaze path calls them in the same order as before, so a second
Pattern language can share the renderer and Art-Net output without copies.

Pre-commit hook checks run manually (hook cannot spawn npx.cmd on Windows/Node 24):
npm run lint, check:e2e-coverage, check:e2e-locators, tsc -b (tsconfig + node),
vitest Preview + renderLoop (36 passed).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
